  "text" : "So the system maps it.\nThis is the quantum value chain from the thing an attacker actually wants, your plaintaste all the way down to raw ore.\nAnd the map shows you something the headline can't the two things genuinely holding quantum back, error corrected logical qubits, and the surface chemistry that ruins them sit over here at Genesis, barely understood.\nNiobium sits over there, practically a commodity already.\nAnd so the honest answer is almost nothing.\nThe purity that actually limits a qubit isn't in the ore, it's an oxide that forms on the chip's own surface from contact with air after the metal is already deposited.\nPure ore doesn't prevent it, so an analyst nudges quantum's velocity from 0.\n05 to 0.\n06.\nProjected position, 0.\n48.\nIt stops short of the line, no boundary crossed.\nNo signal emitted, no pull request.\nThe loudest story of the week changes nothing, and the system says so out loud instead of manufacturing an alarm."
